WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.793
What if your data could make decisions for you?

2
00:00:03.793 --> 00:00:08.450
In this lesson, you will learn to build an if, then, else rule with

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:13.107
a conditional column, edit it to give clearer results, and fix a common error

4
00:00:13.107 --> 00:00:16.100
that appears when a column goes missing. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.237
On the Add Column tab, choose Conditional Column.

6
00:00:21.237 --> 00:00:24.069
It works just like an IF statement:

7
00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:28.520
if a condition is true, return one value. Otherwise, return another.

8
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.278
I name the new column Planning. The rule:

9
00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:43.140
if Units Sold is less than or equal to one thousand, then output zero.

10
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.577
In the Else box, I type:

11
00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:57.000
We will sell this product next year.

12
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.500
So every product that sold more than one thousand units gets this message.

13
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.242
Click OK, and there it is:

14
00:01:21.242 --> 00:01:23.855
the Planning column, at the end of the table.

15
00:01:23.855 --> 00:01:28.500
I move it next to Units Sold, so we can check the rule row by row.

16
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.190
It works!

17
00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.642
Small sellers show zero, and the rest show our message.

18
00:01:56.642 --> 00:02:00.439
But mixing numbers and text in one column is not ideal.

19
00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:01.820
Let's make it better.

20
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.522
I open the step again with the gear icon in Applied Steps, and change

21
00:02:14.522 --> 00:02:17.033
zero to a clear label: STOP SELLING.

22
00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:20.620
Now both results are text, and anyone can read them.

23
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.966
Now, a common trap.

24
00:02:38.966 --> 00:02:41.897
Here a later step still refers to Planning.

25
00:02:41.897 --> 00:02:45.561
Once that column is gone, Power Query shows an error:

26
00:02:45.561 --> 00:02:47.760
the column Planning was not found.

27
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.836
The fix is simple:

28
00:03:01.836 --> 00:03:05.509
delete or edit the step that depends on the missing column.

29
00:03:05.509 --> 00:03:08.180
Now you can solve this error in seconds!

